From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0040] parallel call members over a shared memory

A parallel call runs one function on extra instances of the main module
that share its memory. Members skip the start function, since the host
copies the main instance's globals into them before each run. The fast
interpreter's atomics no longer take the process wide shared memory mutex,
and neither do pointer checks on a shared memory, which never moves.

